**Issue**: #269
**Date**: 2026-08-25
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

@issue-269 @bug @plugin-runtime
Feature: Load project steering through Node inside compiled OMP
  Project-aware nmg-sdlc commands must not treat the compiled extension host
  as the Node interpreter for project steering controllers.

  Scenario: Valid project steering loads under a compiled host
    Given the extension host executable is not Node
    And the project has a valid steering manifest
    When the project prompt registry is built
    Then the steering controller is launched with "node"
    And the project prompt fragments are registered

  Scenario: Draft issue includes project product guidance
    Given the project has valid product steering for "sdlc-draft-issue"
    And the current session is not already in plan mode
    When the user invokes "/sdlc-draft-issue"
    Then the rendered input begins with native "/plan"
    And the rendered prompt includes the project product guidance
    And no "project_runtime_invalid" error is raised

  Scenario: Invalid project steering remains blocked
    Given the project steering controller fails or returns an invalid payload
    When a project-aware command is rendered
    Then rendering fails with "project_runtime_invalid"
    And plugin-only prompt rendering is not used as a fallback

  Scenario: Packaged command works from a disposable project
    Given a disposable project with a valid steering runtime
    And the packaged nmg-sdlc extension is loaded by OMP
    When "/sdlc-draft-issue" is entered through the actual OMP TUI
    Then native plan mode opens without "project_runtime_invalid"
    And no extension error is displayed

  Scenario: Unknown controller example remains context data
    Given runtime context contains "node <plugin-root>/scripts/missing.mjs"
    When the extension materializes available controller paths
    Then the unknown example remains unchanged
    And no "controller unresolved" extension error is raised

  Scenario: Direct missing controller resolution remains strict
    Given a plugin-owned prompt names a packaged controller that does not exist
    When strict controller paths are materialized
    Then resolution fails with "controller_unresolved"

  Scenario: Live consumer smoke passes on valid status output
    Given the public nmg-sdlc smoke repository is available
    And Git and OMP are available
    When the required live smoke provider runs
    Then it loads this checkout in the smoke project
    And exercises "/sdlc-status --json" without mutating the smoke repository
    And passes only when "nextAction.command" begins with "/sdlc-"

  Scenario: Live consumer smoke cannot run
    Given the smoke clone or OMP launch is unavailable
    When the required live smoke provider runs
    Then its effective status is incomplete
    And the required validation is not skipped
